# The panel CSVs are append-only. When two runs both append and one has to
# rebase onto the other, the correct resolution is to keep both sets of lines,
# not to pick a winner. Union does exactly that.
#
# This is safe because every writer already dedupes before appending:
# record_fundamentals refuses a date that is present, record_headlines dedupes
# on link, and record_quotes appends a fresh observed_at each time. So union
# cannot produce a duplicate that the writers would not have produced anyway.
# record_financials appends a second row for a period only to fill a column the
# first left blank, and its readers take the last row for a period.
#
# Union is NOT safe for a rewrite. A file rewritten in place (a schema widening,
# say) and merged against another run's append keeps both copies of every
# line, header included (tested with git 2.x on 2026-09-23). quotes.csv already
# carries a second header from a widening. So a new column in
# data/financials/reported.csv needs a new file or a quiet window, not a widening.
data/**/*.csv merge=union
data/*.csv    merge=union
